You insolent wretch you're
just the idiot who fell for it.

261
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,560
You coward.

262
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:10,780
Rest assured,

263
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:14,217
I'll choose a fitting death for
one who spent her life lying,

264
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,182
deceiving, and betraying others.

265
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:24,580
Before the supreme power of
justice, resistance is futile.

266
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,337
But look on the bright side.

267
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:29,760
At least your friends will
suffer and die with you

268
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:40,300
Hey, what's all that commotion about?

269
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:49,200
Something's coming

270
00:18:01,380 --> 00:18:03,520
Way to go, Sodom and Gomorrah!

271
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:05,220
Keep charging forward!

272
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,700
No! It's them!

273
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:12,817
Those pirates that broke
through the main island's gates!

274
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:13,730
Fire!

275
00:18:13,813 --> 00:18:14,920
Don't let up!

276
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:19,269
Unless you want to die,
get out of the way!

277
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:25,240
Fall back and then restore formation!

278
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,240
Damn, you stupid pirates!

279
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,969
You shouldn't be so cocky!

280
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:39,620
Now I got you, pirate lady!

281
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:52,000
Smooth sailor, these two make it easy.

282
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:55,182
Keep going until we reach
our Captain King Bulls!

283
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:58,790
Hurry!

284
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:01,300
Don't let him escape! He's alone!

285
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:02,540
Surround him!

286
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:05,840
Get out!

287
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:10,980
Get out of my way!

288
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,860
Stupid bastards!

289
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:21,800
Commander, this guy's really scary!

290
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:23,440
Don't falter, men!

291
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:25,840
Bring him down! Attack!

292
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:35,980
There! Yep!

293
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:38,419
That dead end's gotta be the place!

294
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,854
She better not have taken you away yet!

295
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:43,530
Robin!

296
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,380
I suppose that's enough for now.

297
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:51,337
You two, get them out of here.

298
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:52,250
Yes, sir.

299
00:19:52,333 --> 00:19:54,800
There's a C-PRISM stone
lock on her restraints.

300
00:19:55,020 --> 00:19:56,257
Make sure it's secure.

301
00:19:56,340 --> 00:20:00,222
Cutty Flam goes to Impel Down and
Nico Robin to Navy Headquarters.

302
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:04,337
As soon as the ship's ready, we'll
set sail through the Gates of Justice.

303
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:05,250
Right.

304
00:20:05,333 --> 00:20:06,274
It shall be done, sir.

305
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:10,580
Also, take extra
precautions with Cutty Flam.

306
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,860
He can be extremely violent...

307
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:17,280
Has Jaw had been sighted?
Help! Get him off!

308
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:19,077
That request is such a...

309
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:19,990
Yeah.

310
00:20:20,073 --> 00:20:23,074
We got a report about it a
little while back, Cha-ba-ba.

311
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:27,077
When he heard the news, Chief got
so worked up it was embarrassing.

312
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:31,101
They said there were only five
casualties, but that can't be right.

313
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,920
The receiver is off the hook.

314
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:39,477
Don't give us any trouble, tough guy.

315
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:40,501
Let's get going.

316
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:54,400
You can return to your quarters for now.

317
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:58,597
Thanks to this catch, Cape will
be the toast of Navy headquarters.

318
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:03,440
Our status will rise to incredible
heights, in a covert way, of course.

319
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:07,149
And for that, I'd like to propose
a little toast of our own.

320
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:11,766
I'm not in the mood for
some ridiculous toast.

321
00:21:12,060 --> 00:21:15,500
Nor am I interested in our
status or political influence.

322
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:21,412
Our brand of justice is to assassinate
in the name of the world government.

323
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:25,337
As long as they continue to recognize
you as the commander of Cape,

324
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:27,714
we will fulfill our duty to the letter.

325
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:33,420
But we're under no obligation to
support your personal ideologies.

326
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:36,250
That's...

327
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:37,700
that's a sound argument.

328
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:40,780
But then, what is it you want exactly?

329
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:46,780
Perhaps all that we seek is blood.

330
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:00,700
And with CP9, we have
the privilege to kill.

331
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:04,865
These guys give me the creeps.

332
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:10,360
Like he said, they assassinate
legally in the name of justice.

333
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:14,620
And they're very good at what
they do, quite dependable.

334
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:19,257
As long as I have them working for me,
there's nothing I can't accomplish.

335
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:20,440
I'm invincible!

336
00:22:27,940 --> 00:22:29,175
Lieutenant Commander!

337
00:22:29,780 --> 00:22:31,740
Terrible news! What is it?

338
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:33,429
It's Straw Hat Luffy, sir!

339
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:37,660
We can't find him anywhere.

340
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:39,200
He gave us a slip.

341
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,059
That's impossible!

342
00:22:41,340 --> 00:22:43,637
We've got thousands of
Marines here looking for him!

343
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,426
Even so, no one can find him!

344
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:46,620
Don't tell me.

345
00:22:46,820 --> 00:22:49,800
Is he somehow already
inside the courthouse? No!

346
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:53,609
Not even an insect could have
gotten past our defenses, sir!

347
00:22:54,380 --> 00:22:55,210
Go!

348
00:22:55,293 --> 00:22:57,700
We must find Straw Hat at any cost, men!

349
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:07,217
This is the last building.

350
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:08,337
She's gotta be here.

351
00:23:08,420 --> 00:23:09,960
But there isn't a bridge.

352
00:23:10,140 --> 00:23:11,375
Looks kinda far, too.

353
00:23:11,740 --> 00:23:13,800
Well, guess I'll try jumping over.

354
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:20,000
What the heck?

355
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,360
Air door.

356
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:31,950
Hey!

357
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:34,717
You're the bullies working
with that stupid pigeon guy!

358
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:39,437
There seemed to be some discrepancies
between the report and the actual situation.

359
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:40,350
Whoa!

360
00:23:40,433 --> 00:23:42,700
How'd you just appear like that? Awesome!

361
00:23:43,220 --> 00:23:44,050
Magic?

362
00:23:44,133 --> 00:23:46,397
To be honest, it did
seem a little suspicious.

363
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:48,715
No way you only took out five Marines.

364
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:50,840
Man, you really surprised me.

365
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:53,334
An invasion like this is unprecedented.

366
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:56,337
This is the furthest
anyone has ever infiltrated

367
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:58,437
into the mouth of the world government.

368
00:23:58,520 --> 00:24:00,020
But that ends here.

369
00:24:00,340 --> 00:24:03,620
Tell me, how long do you
plan to keep fighting?

370
00:24:17,500 --> 00:24:19,380
Until I die.

371
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:03,580
I don't know.
